[0m[49m[38;5;10m+      9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * C sources: `c_src/` — **READ ONLY, NEVER MODIFY**
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Rust crate: `translation/` (`Cargo.toml`, `src/*.rs`)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     12[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Read `translation/src/jsi.rs` first: it is the translation of `jsi.h`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     13[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `mujs.h`, `utf.h` and `regexp.h` (all structs, all enum constants as
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     14[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `pub const ... : c_int`, all libc bindings). Never redefine anything that
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     15[0m:[38;5;10m[49m already exists there; `use crate::jsi::*;`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## 1. File mapping
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `c_src/src/<name>.c` -> `translation/src/<name>.rs` (same base name).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `json.c` -> `src/json.rs`. Already done: `jsi.rs`, `utf.rs`, `utfdata.rs`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `except.rs`, `vararg.rs`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## 2. Function translation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Non-static** C function (i.e. one that appears in the C `.so` symbol table):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m #[unsafe(no_mangle)]
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pub unsafe extern "C-unwind" fn js_getlength(J: *mut js_State, idx: c_int) -> c_int { unsafe {
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m     ...
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m }}
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Keep the *exact* C name (`utf.h`/`regexp.h` macro renames are already applied
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   in the list you are given: e.g. `regcomp` is really `js_regcomp`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `extern "C-unwind"` (NOT `"C"`): identical ABI but permits the unwinding we
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   use for JS exceptions. Use it for every exported function.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Return `-> !` for functions that never return (`js_throw`, `js_error`, ...)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   only when the C prototype is `JS_NORETURN`; otherwise use the C return type.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **Static** C function:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unsafe fn Ap_join(J: *mut js_State) { unsafe { ... } }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no `no_mangle`, no `extern`, keep the C name verbatim (rename only if it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m collides with a Rust keyword). Static C functions used as `js_CFunction`
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m callbacks must be `unsafe extern "C-unwind" fn(J: *mut js_State)` so they can be
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m stored in a `js_CFunction`:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     52[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     53[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unsafe extern "C-unwind" fn Ap_join(J: *mut js_State) { unsafe { ... } }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     54[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ...
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     55[0m:[38;5;10m[49m jsB_propf(J, c"Array.prototype.join".as_ptr(), Some(Ap_join), 1);
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     56[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     57[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     58[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **File-static data**: `static mut FOO: T = ...;` accessed through
