[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    277[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## 8. Style
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    278[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    279[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Wrap the whole body of each function in one `unsafe { ... }` block, or mark
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    280[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   the fn `unsafe` and add `unsafe {}` inside (Rust 2024 requires explicit
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    281[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `unsafe` blocks inside `unsafe fn`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    282[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * `goto` is common in this codebase. Translate with labelled blocks / loops:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    283[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   ```rust
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    284[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   'readonly: {
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    285[0m:[38;5;10m[49m       ...
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    286[0m:[38;5;10m[49m       if cond { break 'readonly; }   // goto readonly
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    287[0m:[38;5;10m[49m       ...
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    288[0m:[38;5;10m[49m       return;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    289[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    290[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   // readonly:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    291[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   if (*J).strict != 0 { js_typeerror!(...); }
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    292[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   ```
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    293[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   or by factoring the target into a closure/inner fn. Preserve semantics
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    294[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   exactly.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    295[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * C `switch` with fallthrough -> `match` with duplicated arms or if/else chains.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    296[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   When a `switch` has `default:` and labelled cases that fall through, prefer an
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    297[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `if/else` chain to keep the exact behaviour.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    298[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * Do not add bounds checks, null checks, or "fixes" the C does not have.
